52bee8a706c923882bb4055845dfe689f627ef666fadf64523b41650f7bf", "start_line": 110}, {"edge_metadata": {"document_path": "docs/cn/backup_request.md", "layer": "knowledge", "raw_evidence_link_id": "evidence:9c7246aae5187e706bb1407ec25c8d7b4a7e9502c4a3c030db2de01f65c7deb1"}, "end_line": 83, "file_id": null, "generation": 1, "id": "documentsection:dcf07b60c9d54b6886a55e652c19b75f9f8bca778462868f93047202eabf1cff", "kind": "DocumentSection", "language": "markdown", "metadata": {"anchor": "51ec7f3ff1e31ea8", "content_hash": "7b05be8559713d153b25b1c43f3e53269b5494018a0927877f19212628fe2916", "document_id": "document:a65e374b63cd70e248f824edc65857111704ce567ad11bd32e222318d629940d", "document_type": "Document", "document_version": 109941659600342, "end_line": 83, "explicit_id": null, "heading_path": "�����server���Թ���һ������������ʱ / Backup Request ���� / ʹ��������������", "layer": "knowledge", "path": "docs/cn/backup_request.md", "start_line": 48, "text": "### ʹ��������������\n\n���� `CreateRateLimitedBackupPolicy` �����������ԣ����������õ� `ChannelOptions.backup_request_policy`��\n\n```c++\n#include \"brpc/backup_request_policy.h\"\n#include <memory>\n\nbrpc::RateLimitedBackupPolicyOptions opts;\nopts.backup_request_ms = 10;       // ����10msδ����ʱ����backup����\nopts.max_backup_ratio = 0.3;       // backup�����������30%\nopts.window_size_seconds = 10;     // �������ڿ��ȣ��룩\nopts.update_interval_seconds = 5;  // ���������ˢ�¼�����룩\n\n// CreateRateLimitedBackupPolicy���ص�ָ���ɵ��÷������ͷš�\n// policy���������ڱ��볤��channel����������channel��������policy��\nstd::unique_ptr<brpc::BackupRequestPolicy> policy(\n    brpc::CreateRateLimitedBackupPolicy(opts));\n\nbrpc::ChannelOptions options;\noptions.backup_request_policy = policy.get(); // Channel��ӵ�иö���\nchannel.Init(..., &options);\n// channel������policy����֮ǰ���١�\n```\n\n����˵����`RateLimitedBackupPolicyOptions`����\n\n| �ֶ� | Ĭ��ֵ | ˵�� |\n|------|--------|------|\n| `backup_request_ms` | -1 | ��ʱ��ֵ�����룩��-1 ��ʾ�̳� `ChannelOptions.backup_request_ms`������ͨ�� `ChannelOptions.backup_request_policy` ���ò���ʱ��Ч��ͨ�� Controller ע��ʱû�� channel ���Ļ���ֵ��Ӧ��ʽָ�� >= 0 ��ֵ�������� >= -1�� |\n| `max_backup_ratio` | 0.1 | backup�������ޣ�ȡֵ��Χ (0, 1] |\n| `window_size_seconds` | 10 | �������ڿ��ȣ��룩��ȡֵ��Χ [1, 3600] |\n| `update_interval_seconds` | 5 | ����ˢ�¼�����룩������ >= 1 |\n\n�������Ϸ�ʱ `CreateRateLimitedBackupPolicy` ���� `nullptr`��\n", "title": "ʹ��������������"}, "name": "ʹ��������������", "qualified_name": "docs/cn/backup_request.md#51ec7f3ff1e31ea8", "relation": "DOCUMENTS", "repo_id": "repo:074b46c6e95703171fcd66ba04121d7fcacc04ef0fa2e0085f37e49cc4137eac", "shard_id": null, "signature": null, "source_hash": "7b05be8559713d153b25b1c43f3e53269b5494018a0927877f19212628fe2916", "start_line": 48}, {"edge_metadata": {"document_path": "docs/en/backup_request.md", "layer": "knowledge", "raw_evidence_link_id": "evidence:d27df2fca1c8562aee300df94a5ae94d3809a7fbc3976ae435adc1026a16c2c3"}, "end_line": 115, "file_id": null, "generation": 1, "id": "documentsection:3d62a08bb9b2a563d709cd06ff30d649b13ff402670fde4f97b274902b020c25", "kind": "DocumentSection", "language": "markdown", "metadata": {"anchor": "3ae852dd98434bdd", "content_hash": "eeb8a712eae30b47124742ea0ec59bf720e64fa3761c851421adf831bc9b3564", "document_id": "document:c0778cb30f8a1417562a237ffcf4d7656e8170fdd20a696923b7b5ec93ccb2f3", "document_type": "Document", "document_version": 108798212291126, "end_line": 115, "explicit_id": null, "heading_path": "When backend servers can be hung in a naming service / Rate-limited backup requests / Implementation notes", "layer": "knowledge", "path": "docs/en/backup_request.md", "start_line": 110, "text": "### Implementation notes\n\n- The ratio is computed over a sliding time window using bvar counters. The cached value is refreshed at most once per `update_interval_seconds` using a lock-free CAS election, so the overhead per RPC is very low (two atomic loads in the common path).\n- Backup decisions are counted immediately at decision time (before the RPC completes) to provide faster feedback during latency spikes. Total RPCs are counted on completion. This means the ratio may transiently lag during a spike, but this is intentional �� the limiter is designed for approximate, best-effort throttling, not exact enforcement.\n- Each channel using rate limiting maintains two `bvar::Window` sampler tasks. Keep this in mind in deployments with a very large number of channels.\n", "title": "Implementation notes"}, "name": "Implementation notes", "qualified_name": "docs/en/backup_request.md#3ae852dd98434bdd", "relation": "DOCUMENTS", "repo_id": "repo:074b46c6e95703171fcd66ba04121d7fcacc04ef0fa2e0085f37e49cc4137eac", "shard_id": null, "signature": null, "source_hash": "eeb8a712eae30b47124742ea0ec59bf720e64fa3761c851421adf831bc9b3564", "start_line": 110}, {"edge_metadata": {"document_path": "docs/en/backup_request.md", "layer": "knowledge", "raw_evidence_link_id": "evidence:43ded9e9e6e68cf4fe237d6c4045fe33d1c2c29524197f1f7c0cfbe9ab7d883c"}, "end_line": 83, "file_id": null, "generation": 1, "id": "documentsection:987ee30623980271e8c1c6343f5c2629c73f7b00168896845e941fe8772eb2e1", "kind": "DocumentSection", "language": "markdown", "metadata": {"anchor": "c2468c9d42c0dc4c", "content_hash": "0856cd97edcf079acd24645de92589ccec2c0dd4a70b42aceb8e5c4532edd896", "document_id": "document:c0778cb30f8a1417562a237ffcf4d7656e8170fdd20a696923b7b5ec93ccb2f3", "document_type": "Document", "document_version": 108798212291126, "end_line": 83, "explicit_id": null, "heading_path": "When backend servers can be hung in a naming service / Rate-limited backup requests / Using the built-in rate-limiting policy", "layer": "knowledge", "path": "docs/en/backup_request.md", "start_line": 48, "text": "### Using the built-in rate-limiting policy\n\nCall `CreateRateLimitedBackupPolicy` and set the result on `ChannelOptions.backup_request_policy`:\n\n```c++\n#include \"brpc/backup_request_policy.h\"\n#include <memory>\n\nbrpc::RateLimitedBackupPolicyOptions opts;\nopts.backup_request_ms = 10;       // send backup if RPC does not complete within 10ms\nopts.max_backup_ratio = 0.3;       // cap backup requests at 30% of total\nopts.window_size_seconds = 10;     // sliding window width in seconds\nopts.update_interval_seconds = 5;  // how often the cached ratio is refreshed\n\n// The caller owns the returned pointer.\n// The policy must outlive the channel �� destroy the channel before the policy.\nstd::unique_ptr<brpc::BackupRequestPolicy> policy(\n    brpc::CreateRateLimitedBackupPolicy(opts));\n\nbrpc::ChannelOptions options;\noptions.backup_request_policy = policy.get(); // NOT owned by channel\nchannel.Init(..., &options);\n// channel must be destroyed before policy goes out of scope.\n```\n\n`RateLimitedBackupPolicyOptions` fields:\n\n| Field | Default | Description |\n|-------|---------|-------------|\n| `backup_request_ms` | -1 | Timeout threshold in ms. -1 means inherit from `ChannelOptions.backup_request_ms` (only works when the policy is set via `ChannelOptions.backup_request_policy`; at controller level there is no channel-level fallback, so set an explicit >= 0 value instead). Must be >= -1. |\n| `max_backup_ratio` | 0.1 | Max backup ratio; range (0, 1] |\n| `window_size_seconds` | 10 | Sliding window width in seconds; range [1, 3600] |\n| `update_interval_seconds` | 5 | Cached-ratio refresh interval in seconds; must be >= 1 |\n\n`CreateRateLimitedBackupPolicy` returns `nullptr` if any parameter is invalid.\n", "title": "Using the built-in rate-limiting policy"}, "name": "Using the built-in rate-limiting policy", "qualified_name": "docs/en/backup_request.md#c2468c9d42c0dc4c", "relation": "DOCUMENTS", "repo_id": "repo:074b46c6e95703171fcd66ba04121d7fcacc04ef0fa2e0085f37e49cc4137eac", "shard_id": null, "signature": null, "source_hash": "0856cd97edcf079acd24645de92589ccec2c0dd4a70b42aceb8e5c4532edd896", "start_line": 48}], "returned_evidence_count": 10, "returned_evidence_ids": ["E-CODE-95e2b12098d2b3e4abea769b", "E-XLINK-8c53d0b57aa40968e9c8ba17", "E-XLINK-94055898215a0b82739dc237", "E-XLINK-e3fe9b3d924d68f482bd290f", "E-XLINK-f4c89a2e0346fb42c4ba8a91", "E-DOC-3d047e723af4c7446012da31", "E-DOC-9d9674320ddc2684f8d2773a", "E-DOC-c46e94bb27b9f6c2c25be8ab", "E-DOC-f64718932994b6e536e183ab", "E-SHARD-f41b84349e240f582882c51c"], "summary": "Method brpc.RateLimitedBackupPolicyOptions.update_interval_seconds ()", "supporting_evidence": [{"commit": "ae09e960c7291605dda52356cc0c2d45567fb53e", "confidence": 0.7, "evidence_id": "E-XLINK-8c53d0b57aa40968e9c8ba17", "generation": 1, "kind": "CROSS_LAYER_LINK", "metadata": {"bundle_profile": "module_understanding", "bundle_role": "SUPPORTING", "bundle_seed_role": "SUPPORTING", "direct": true, "distance": 1, "document_path": "docs/en/backup_request.md", "fact_id": "edge:9d2e3dcae2034f36b26d6beeb133d53f03f3daf98f6763e9f8833c4e2111d85a", "layer": "knowledge", "raw_evidence_link_id": "evidence:43ded9e9e6e68cf4fe237d6c4045fe33d1c2c29524197f1f7c0cfbe9ab7d883c", "resolution_status": "resolved"}, "provenance": "explicit_symbol_reference", "relation": "DOCUMENTS", "repository": "repo:074b46c6e95703171fcd66ba04121d7fcacc04ef0fa2e0085f37e49cc4137eac", "source_id": "documentsection:987ee30623980271e8c1c6343f5c2629c73f7b00168896845e941fe8772eb2e1", "source_path": "docs/en/backup_request.md", "source_range": {"end_line": 83, "start_line": 48}, "summary": "docs/en/backup_request.md#c2468c9d42c0dc4c DOCUMENTS brpc.RateLimitedBackupPolicyOptions.update_interval_seconds", "target_id": "symbol:c6cd0bb6f23db23ed3fe354cd5b9c5bb4a5e05587f94c9364b81834dbef98efc"}, {"commit": "ae09e960c7291605dda52356cc0c2d45567fb53e", "confidence": 0.7, "evidence_id": "E-XLINK-94055898215a0b82739dc237", "generation": 1, "kind": "CROSS_LAYER_LINK", "metadata": {"bundle_profile": "module_understanding", "bundle_role": "SUPPORTING", "bundle_seed_role": "SUPPORTING", "direct": true, "distance": 1, "document_path": "docs/cn